{%- comment -%}
  vf-editorial.liquid

  Reusable editorial-register page template surface. Bone register.
  Renders page.title as the H1 and page.content as the body, wrapped
  in the Materials-page visual chrome.

  Visual mirror of vf-materials but reads page.content instead of
  schema fields. vf-materials is page-specific (production methodology,
  hardcoded five-section structure); vf-editorial is reusable across
  any editorial-register page whose body content lives in admin
  Content rather than in template-specific schema (Care · Cleaning,
  Process, Shipping, Returns, future editorial pages).

  URL pattern: any page whose template is set to "editorial" in the
  Shopify admin Page → Template dropdown.

  All visible body content lives in the page's admin Content field —
  no section settings, no schema-driven copy. Empty Content renders
  the visual chrome without errors.

  Optional page metafields (namespace vox — CLAUDE.md §9 — the vf
  prefix is <3 chars and rejected by Shopify at save time):
    vox.eyebrow  (single_line_text_field) — via .value (string),
                                            passed to snippets/vf-eyebrow
    vox.headline (single_line_text_field) — via .value (string),
                                            replaces page.title on the h1
    vox.intro    (rich_text_field)        — kept as the whole metafield
                                            object (no .value) and
                                            rendered explicitly via
                                            | metafield_tag so Shopify
                                            emits real <p> tags with
                                            inline markup, matching
                                            vf-contact's multi-paragraph
                                            spec. Explicit filter drops
                                            the implicit-metafield-
                                            render assumption. Blank
                                            check uses vf_intro.value
                                            != blank so an unset (nil)
                                            metafield falls through to
                                            the bare-h1 branch and never
                                            triggers the header wrapper.
  When all three are blank / nil, the bare <h1>page.title</h1> renders
  exactly as it did before the metafields were wired (pixel-identical
  fallback — verified against preprod tip 088e5604).

  Schema contract: docs/section-schemas.md (§10 pending)
  CSS: assets/vf-tokens.css §21
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign vf_eyebrow       = page.metafields.vox.eyebrow.value
  assign vf_headline_meta = page.metafields.vox.headline.value
  assign vf_intro         = page.metafields.vox.intro

  if vf_headline_meta != blank
    assign vf_headline = vf_headline_meta
  else
    assign vf_headline = page.title
  endif

  assign vf_has_header_extras = false
  if vf_eyebrow != blank or vf_headline_meta != blank or vf_intro.value != blank
    assign vf_has_header_extras = true
  endif
-%}

<section class="vf-editorial" data-mode="bone">
  <div class="vf-editorial__inner page-width page-width--narrow">

    {%- if vf_has_header_extras -%}
      <header class="vf-editorial__header">
        {%- if vf_eyebrow != blank -%}
          {%- render 'vf-eyebrow', text: vf_eyebrow -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        <h1 class="vf-editorial__headline">{{ vf_headline | escape }}</h1>
        {%- if vf_intro.value != blank -%}
          <div class="vf-editorial__intro">{{ vf_intro | metafield_tag }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </header>
      {%- if vf_intro.value != blank -%}
        <hr class="vf-editorial__rule" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <h1 class="vf-editorial__headline">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if page.content != blank -%}
      <div class="vf-editorial__content">
        {{ page.content }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "VF Editorial",
  "class": "vf-editorial-section",
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["page"] },
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
